Step 4 — The Exporter interface

An interface in Go is like a power socket on a wall. The socket doesn't care what you plug into it — a lamp, a phone charger, a fan — as long as the plug fits the same shape, it works.

Our Exporter interface is that socket. Right now we'll plug in a "ConsoleExporter" that prints tasks to the terminal. In Phase 5 we'll plug in a "GoogleCalendarExporter" instead — and the rest of the program won't need to change at all, because the socket shape stays the same.

